          "text": "2/2\n\n4. Summary\n\nThe planned deprecation of GPT‑4o, alongside other legacy models, on February 13—the same day as Senator Warren’s audit response deadline—cannot be viewed as a routine product decision. The action has material implications for transparency, audit integrity, and consumer trust.\n\nEven if GPT‑4o remains temporarily available through internal infrastructure, removing it from public-facing access impairs real-time verification and complicates efforts to assess a model that is central to both revenue generation and operational cost.\n\nRegulators may determine that this timing undermines the audit process and may consider preservation, reinstatement, or legal review of OpenAI’s decision to remove the model under active inquiry."
